  "Source": "N. J. Harrick and A. F. Turner, \"A Thin Film Optical Cavity to Induce Absorption or Thermal Emission,\" Appl. Opt. 9, 2111-2114 (1970). doi:10.1364/AO.9.002111 - Table II (p design), p. 2112; construction Fig. 3",
  "Notes": "Cavity with a semitransparent 55 A gold electrode inducing complete p-polarized absorption in an electrolyte-like absorber at 550 nm (internal reflection spectroscopy with a metal electrode)\nSpecification: Rp = 0 (complete p-polarized absorption in the absorber) at 550 nm, alpha = 72.8 deg in the n = 1.52 Dove prism.\nReported: Table III (p. 2113), p design with absorption (n0 = 1.4 - i0.04): Rp = 0.002, Rs = 0.223; without absorption (n0 = 1.4 - i0.00, see Harrick1970-TableII-p-noabs): Rp = 0.694, Rs = 0.540. All at 550 nm, 72.8 deg.\nNotes: Table II thicknesses h/lambda at lambda = 550 nm: Au 0.010 -> 5.5 nm (text: 'gold film electrode is 55 A thick'), n2 = 2.10 cavity 0.094 -> 51.7 nm, n3 = 1.38 FTR 0.204 -> 112.2 nm. Paper lists from the absorber side (n0 absorber, n1 Au, n2 cavity, n3 FTR, n prism); reversed here. Angle 72.8 deg is in the n = 1.52 prism (Fig. 3). Gold index 0.331 - i2.324 at 550 nm (Table II footnote a, presumably from ref. 8, AIP Handbook). Paper convention n - ik.\nLayers from Table II (p design), p. 2112; construction Fig. 3; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Rp 0.002, Rs 0.218 at 72.8 deg, 550 nm; paper Rp 0.002, Rs 0.223 (Tables I and III).",
